<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><caml:MeasureDoc version="1.0" xsi:schemaLocation="http://lc.ca.gov/legalservices/schemas/caml.1# xca.1.xsd" xmlns:caml="http://lc.ca.gov/legalservices/schemas/caml.1#" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xmlns:xhtml="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance">
<!-- Copyright © Legislative Counsel Bureau, State of California. -->
<caml:Description xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><caml:Id>20250SB__121298AMD</caml:Id><caml:VersionNum>98</caml:VersionNum><caml:History><caml:Action><caml:ActionText>INTRODUCED</caml:ActionText><caml:ActionDate>2026-02-19</caml:ActionDate></caml:Action><caml:Action><caml:ActionText>AMENDED_SENATE</caml:ActionText><caml:ActionDate>2026-03-25</caml:ActionDate></caml:Action></caml:History><caml:LegislativeInfo><caml:SessionYear>2025</caml:SessionYear><caml:SessionNum>0</caml:SessionNum><caml:MeasureType>SB</caml:MeasureType><caml:MeasureNum>1212</caml:MeasureNum><caml:MeasureState>AMD</caml:MeasureState></caml:LegislativeInfo><caml:AuthorText authorType="LEAD_AUTHOR">Introduced by Senator Jones</caml:AuthorText><caml:Authors><caml:Legislator><caml:Contribution>LEAD_AUTHOR</caml:Contribution><caml:House>SENATE</caml:House><caml:Name>Jones</caml:Name></caml:Legislator></caml:Authors><caml:Title><?xm-deletion_mark data="An act to amend Section 16 of the Penal Code, relating to criminal law. "?><?xm-insertion_mark_start?>An act to amend Section 653o of the Penal Code, relating to criminal law.<?xm-insertion_mark_end?></caml:Title><caml:RelatingClause>criminal law</caml:RelatingClause><caml:GeneralSubject><caml:Subject><?xm-deletion_mark data="Criminal law. "?><?xm-insertion_mark_start?>Endangered wildlife: kangaroos.<?xm-insertion_mark_end?></caml:Subject></caml:GeneralSubject><caml:DigestText><?xm-insertion_mark_start?><p>Existing law makes it a misdemeanor to import into the state for commercial purposes, to possess with intent to sell, or to sell within the state the dead body, or a part or product thereof, of a polar bear, leopard, ocelot, tiger, cheetah, jaguar, sable antelope, wolf, zebra, whale, cobra, python, sea turtle, colobus monkey, kangaroo, vicuna, sea otter, free-roaming feral horse, dolphin or porpoise, Spanish lynx, or elephant.</p><p>This bill would exempt from that prohibition the import into the state for commercial purposes, possession with intent to sell, or sale within the state of kangaroos if they are harvested in accordance with Australian law, the federal Endangered Species Act, and applicable international conventions, as specified.</p><?xm-insertion_mark_end?><?xm-deletion_mark data="&lt;xhtml:p>Existing law specifies that crimes and public offenses include felonies, misdemeanors, and infractions.&lt;/xhtml:p>&lt;xhtml:p>This bill would make technical, nonsubstantive changes to that provision.&lt;/xhtml:p>"?></caml:DigestText><caml:DigestKey><caml:VoteRequired>MAJORITY</caml:VoteRequired><caml:Appropriation>NO</caml:Appropriation><caml:FiscalCommittee><?xm-deletion_mark data="NO"?><?xm-insertion_mark_start?>YES<?xm-insertion_mark_end?></caml:FiscalCommittee><caml:LocalProgram>NO</caml:LocalProgram></caml:DigestKey><caml:MeasureIndicators><caml:ImmediateEffect>NO</caml:ImmediateEffect><caml:ImmediateEffectFlags><caml:Urgency>NO</caml:Urgency><caml:TaxLevy>NO</caml:TaxLevy><caml:Election>NO</caml:Election><caml:UsualCurrentExpenses>NO</caml:UsualCurrentExpenses><caml:BudgetBill>NO</caml:BudgetBill><caml:Prop25TrailerBill>NO</caml:Prop25TrailerBill></caml:ImmediateEffectFlags></caml:MeasureIndicators></caml:Description><caml:Bill id="bill" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><caml:Preamble>The people of the State of California do enact as follows:</caml:Preamble><caml:BillSection id="id_E9EB2282-716C-4341-84F8-6D9BD70E46A9"><caml:Num><?xm-insertion_mark_start?>SECTION 1.<?xm-insertion_mark_end?></caml:Num><caml:ActionLine action="IS_AMENDED" xlink:href="urn:caml:codes:PEN:caml#xpointer(%2Fcaml%3ALawDoc%2Fcaml%3ACode%2Fcaml%3ALawHeading%5B%40type%3D'PART'%20and%20caml%3ANum%3D'1.'%5D%2Fcaml%3ALawHeading%5B%40type%3D'TITLE'%20and%20caml%3ANum%3D'15.'%5D%2Fcaml%3ALawHeading%5B%40type%3D'CHAPTER'%20and%20caml%3ANum%3D'2.'%5D%2Fcaml%3ALawSection%5Bcaml%3ANum%3D'653o.'%5D)" xlink:label="fractionType: LAW_SECTION" xlink:type="locator"><?xm-insertion_mark_start?>Section 653o of the <caml:DocName>Penal Code</caml:DocName> is amended to read:<?xm-insertion_mark_end?></caml:ActionLine><caml:Fragment><caml:LawSection id="id_C6CAAC0A-D2ED-4676-9D9B-493E0343E47F"><caml:Num>653o.</caml:Num><caml:LawSectionVersion id="id_FDDBA086-3726-4C96-B820-37BA7492682B"><caml:Content><p>(a)<span class="EnSpace"/><?xm-insertion_mark_start?>(1)<?xm-insertion_mark_end?><?xm-insertion_mark_start?><span class="EnSpace"/><?xm-insertion_mark_end?> It is unlawful to import into this state for commercial purposes, to possess with intent to sell, or to sell within the state, the dead body, or a part or product thereof, of a polar bear, leopard, ocelot, tiger, cheetah, jaguar, sable antelope, wolf (Canis lupus), zebra, whale, cobra, python, sea turtle, colobus monkey, kangaroo,<?xm-insertion_mark_start?> except as provided in paragraph (2),<?xm-insertion_mark_end?> vicuna, sea otter, free-roaming feral horse, dolphin or porpoise (Delphinidae), Spanish lynx, or elephant.</p><?xm-insertion_mark_start?><p>(2)<span class="EnSpace"/>Kangaroos exempted under this paragraph shall be wild harvested pursuant to Australian federal, state, and territory law, the federal Endangered Species Act (16 U.S.C. Sec. 1531 et seq.), and applicable international conventions.</p><?xm-insertion_mark_end?><p>(b)<span class="EnSpace"/>(1)<span class="EnSpace"/>Commencing January 1, 2020, it is unlawful to import into this state for commercial purposes, to possess with intent to sell, or to sell within the state, the dead body, or a part or product thereof, of a crocodile or alligator.</p><p>(2)<span class="EnSpace"/>This subdivision does not authorize the importation or sale of any alligator or crocodilian species, or products thereof, that are listed as endangered under the federal Endangered Species Act, or to allow the importation or sale of any alligator or crocodilian species, or products thereof, in violation of
						federal law or international treaty to which the United States is a party.</p><p>(c)<span class="EnSpace"/>Commencing January 1, 2022, it is unlawful to import into this state for commercial purposes, to possess with intent to sell, or to sell within the state, the dead body, or any part or product thereof, of an iguana, skink, caiman, hippopotamus, or a Teju, Ring, or Nile lizard.</p><p>(d)<span class="EnSpace"/>A person who violates this section is guilty of a misdemeanor and shall be subject to a fine of not less than one thousand dollars ($1,000) and not to exceed five thousand dollars ($5,000) or imprisonment in the county jail not to exceed six months, or both that fine and imprisonment, for each violation.</p><p>(e)<span class="EnSpace"/>The prohibitions against importation for commercial purposes, possession with intent to sell, and sale of the species listed in this section are severable. A
						finding of the invalidity of any one or more prohibitions shall not affect the validity of any remaining prohibitions.</p></caml:Content></caml:LawSectionVersion></caml:LawSection></caml:Fragment></caml:BillSection><?xm-deletion_mark data="&lt;caml:BillSection id=&quot;id_8938952F-3D11-4402-8558-34D683947ED7&quot;>&lt;caml:Num>SECTION 1.&lt;/caml:Num>&lt;caml:ActionLine action=&quot;IS_AMENDED&quot; xlink:href=&quot;urn:caml:codes:PEN:caml#xpointer(%2Fcaml%3ALawDoc%2Fcaml%3ACode%2Fcaml%3ALawHeading%2Fcaml%3ALawSection%5Bcaml%3ANum%3D&apos;16.&apos;%5D)&quot; xlink:label=&quot;fractionType: LAW_SECTION&quot; xlink:type=&quot;locator&quot;>Section 16 of the &lt;caml:DocName>Penal Code&lt;/caml:DocName> is amended to read:&lt;/caml:ActionLine>&lt;caml:Fragment>&lt;caml:LawSection id=&quot;id_85AE9A16-2D8D-4637-950A-76AAFFCEC8D2&quot;>&lt;caml:Num>16.&lt;/caml:Num>&lt;caml:LawSectionVersion id=&quot;id_E00AC45F-9191-46C2-880C-5C8665CA7163&quot;>&lt;caml:Content>&lt;xhtml:p>Crimes and public offenses include all of the following:&lt;/xhtml:p>&lt;xhtml:p>(a)&lt;xhtml:span class=&quot;EnSpace&quot;/>Felonies.&lt;/xhtml:p>&lt;xhtml:p>(b)&lt;xhtml:span class=&quot;EnSpace&quot;/>Misdemeanors.&lt;/xhtml:p>&lt;xhtml:p>(c)&lt;xhtml:span class=&quot;EnSpace&quot;/>Infractions.&lt;/xhtml:p>&lt;/caml:Content>&lt;/caml:LawSectionVersion>&lt;/caml:LawSection>&lt;/caml:Fragment>&lt;/caml:BillSection>"?></caml:Bill></caml:MeasureDoc>